{"step_index":220,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T03:47:31Z","thinking":"Examining lines 517, 570, 105, 377, and 391, `HEADER_HEIGHT` consistently resolves to 50px. This value influences the positioning and height of visual elements within the Gantt chart, specifically the absolute positioning and the division lines.\n\n\nThe `divide-y` class combined with fixed row heights and potential content wrapping is causing vertical misalignment, specifically due to the addition of a 1px top border on each subsequent row after the first. The text wrapping in the header row increases its height, which then shifts the entire chart down because the `HEADER_HEIGHT` is fixed. The padding and `py-1` on children inside `flex items-center` can cause the row to stretch too if font size + line height + padding > 44px. The misalignment accumulates with each row due to the `divide-y` border.\n\nTo address this, adjusting `HEADER_HEIGHT` to 52px and `ROW_HEIGHT` to 44px provides the necessary space for the header content and mitigates the wrapping issue, preventing the chart's vertical shift.\n```jsx\n<div\n    className=\"sticky top-0 z-40 bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex items-center text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 uppercase tracking-wider\n    h-[HEADER_HEIGHT]\n>\n    // Header Content\n</div>\n```\n\n\nThe left header's total width is calculated as 648px, utilizing a fixed layout with `whitespace-nowrap truncate` to prevent text wrapping, thus ensuring a fixed header height of 52px. Both the left and right headers now have a fixed height, which helps prevent vertical misalignment. This 52px height is enforced on both header sections.\n\n\nEliminating `divide-y` on left rows is necessary; it conflicts with the explicit row heights and causes unwanted borders between elements. The correct approach is to set the `ROW_HEIGHT` to 44px and remove the `divide-y` class